<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">European colonial expansion</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">European colonial expansion describes the growth of European empires overseas from the fifteenth to the twentieth century, through trade, conquest and settlement. It undermined or destroyed many states, as in the British conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>, French conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> and the partition of Central African states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a>.</p></div>
